=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 invariants:

I1 default-off: registry entry sets DefaultOn: false; the
  cabin-temperature-impact-narrative toggle starts off in
  Settings.aifeatures and the user must explicitly opt in.

I3 baseline intact: TemperatureImpactPage continues to render the
  deterministic VehicleSelect, ScatterChart, bucket breakdown,
  optimal-temperature analysis, and recommendations regardless of
  ai_mode. The AI section is added ABOVE the MetricCards grid so
  that when AI is on it contextualises the chart, and when AI is
  off the page renders identically to its pre-slice form (the
  withAiFeature HOC returns null when the gate is closed).

I4 zero egress: the AI route is only ever invoked when the user
  clicks the Narrate button inside a gated component that is
  ABSENT in off mode (gated by withAiFeature, validated in
  TestCabinTemperatureNarrativeAIOffShowsChartsOnly). The provider
  call is routed through the dispatcher's locked decorator chain
  (redaction → rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace) inherited
  from F0-F9 foundations.

I5 hidden UI: withAiFeature('cabin-temperature-impact-narrative',
  …) returns null when the per-feature toggle is off OR ai_mode is
  off. The off-mode Vitest asserts container.toBeEmptyDOMElement()
  AND queryByTestId('ai-feature-cabin-temperature-impact-narrative-root')
  not.toBeInTheDocument(). The positive control (ai_mode='cloud',
  toggle=true) confirms the gate is wired correctly.

I6 404 routes: every call site of the new POST handler is wrapped
  in g.Wrap("cabin-temperature-impact-narrative", …) inside
  mountAIRoutes (internal/api/ai_routes.go). The Go test
  TestCabinTemperatureNarrativeAIOffShowsChartsOnly inside
  ai_temperature_impact_handler_test.go asserts the registered
  route returns 404 when ai_mode='off'.

I7 per-feature: the registry entry is opt-in (DefaultOn false) and
  the gate inspects BOTH ai_mode AND ai_features['cabin-…']. The
  positive-control test fixes both keys; the off-mode tests prove
  the AND logic: mode=off OR toggle=false hides the surface.

I10 type system: the tool envelope (TemperatureImpact /
  TemperatureImpactBucket / TemperatureImpactMonth) is a single
  Go struct with explicit JSON tags. The handler-side parser
  validates vehicle_id > 0; the strategy whitelist hard-pins
  query_temperature_impact as the only callable tool.

I12 client/bg: this slice adds:
   - Service worker chunk:  ai-cabin-temperature-impact-narrative
     (registry routes metadata; documented in slice prompt §
     "Off-mode contract impact"). The webpack/Vite chunk emits only
     when the lazy import of AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative is
     reached, which itself only happens when the gated render path
     is taken (off mode never imports the chunk).
   - Background jobs:       none.
   - Push kinds:            none.
   - Client storage keys:   none.

Why selection mechanism is at COMPOSITION time, not inside
business logic: the AI component is a sibling of the deterministic
content under the same PageContainer, gated by withAiFeature at
the JSX level. No branching inside the data-fetch or chart-render
paths exists — the deterministic chart code is unchanged.

Why the strategy uses PolicyDigest-shaped redaction: the surface
narrates user-named vehicles aggregating their drives. ClassVehicleName
must round-trip in ModeRedactedTags so the narration can quote
"vehicle X" without leaking driver-pii or trip locations. Trip and
location classes remain tagged + non-round-trip — same shape as
PolicyDigest. The new policy
PolicyCabinTemperatureImpactNarrative() lives next to its sibling
PolicyPreheatPrecoolRecommender() in policies.go.

Why a single tool query_temperature_impact (no helper extraction):
the slice prompt explicitly forbids "duplicate WRITE paths" but
admits read-path duplication when extracting a shared helper would
risk regressing the canonical baseline route. The
AITemperatureImpactSource adapter runs the SAME aggregation SQL
TempImpactHandler.Get already runs — no parallel write path; the
LLM never persists.

